  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive verb ({他動詞|たどうし}). The person/thing being mocked takes を.\n\nRELATED FORMS:\n・{嘲|あざけ}り - mockery, ridicule (noun)\n・{嘲笑|ちょうしょう} - derision, mockery (Sino-Japanese compound)\n\nCOMPARISON:\n・{嘲|あざけ}る - to mock, ridicule (contemptuous)\n・からかう - to tease (often playful)\n・{馬鹿|ばか}にする - to make a fool of, look down on\n・{冷|ひ}やかす - to tease, make fun of\n\nUSAGE:\nThis word has a negative connotation, implying contempt or cruelty. It's stronger than からかう (to tease).",
